According to a report by Intel Market Research, global Knowledge Management Software market was valued at USD 16 billion in 2025 and is projected to grow to USD 32 billion by 2034, registering a robust compound annual growth rate of 9 % during the forecast period (2026 2034). The upward trajectory reflects heightened demand for scalable digital tools that capture, organise and disseminate organisational knowledge.
Knowledge Management Software (KMS) encompasses platforms that capture, organise, share and retrieve an organisation’s collective expertise and information assets. These solutions typically integrate document repositories, collaboration tools, search engines, analytics modules and AI‐powered recommendation engines to enable employees to locate relevant insights rapidly and contribute new knowledge efficiently.
